WEBVTT

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.600
For grocery, press six.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:14.950
[Keypad tone]

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.340
Grocery, this is Marco.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:21.120
Hey, Marco, it's Riley with Tumbleweed
Pretzels and Sunvale Sparkling.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:22.560
I know you're busy, so I'll be quick.

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:27.180
Our Garlic Parmesan pretzel twists, uh, they
haven't sold in two weeks.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.680
Could you check if they're on the shelf,
please?

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.970
Your grapefruit keeps cutting, uh, or rather
getting cut on me.

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:37.920
Um, should I just drop it?

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.360
Ooh, no, that's, um, that's just a warehouse
issue.

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.530
A damaged load was refused,
— Ah, okay.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.760
so nothing on your end.

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:49.620
Uh, it's back Tuesday,
— Got it. Okay.

00:00:49.630 --> 00:00:51.410
and on Thursday's trucks.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.140
So please keep the tag up, and your open
orders will fill.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.450
Hey, Marco, it's Riley with Tumbleweed
Pretzels

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:06.840
and Sunvale Sparkling, following up on Monday.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.160
Hey, this is Sam at Brookside.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:14.140
Uh, Marco's off today, and I just got your
message about the truck.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.310
Hi, Sam. Thanks for calling us back.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.130
I was checking whether the Garlic Parmesan,
Lime, and Grapefruit

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:23.060
from this morning's truck made it to the
shelf. Did they?
